{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_plan_implementation_plan", "label": "Implementation Plan: Contract Rule Folder and File Rename", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_plan_three_phase_fasing", "label": "Three-Phase Phasing (folder, files 01-03, files 04-06)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The folder is the first demonstrable checkpoint and the two groups of three files are cohesive increments, so each phase can be validated in isolation; Phase 2 depends on Phase 1 only for the folder path, and Phase 3 depends on both only for the final zero-old-names sweep."}, {"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_plan_constitution_check", "label": "Constitution Check Gate (PASS rationale)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All six principles pass because the change is nominal: no new flag or extension artifact (I, II), no generated Java or template change (III), no externalized configuration (IV), no credentials (V), and validation reinstalls the artifact instead of blaming code (VI); the legacy redirect keeps its old name deliberately under Principle II."}, {"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_plan_negative_regression_checks", "label": "Negative Regression Checks (provoked change -> expected failing suite)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mapping each possible regression to the suite that must fail proves the suites actually guard the feature rather than merely passing."}, {"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_plan_structure_decision", "label": "Structure Decision (single Maven module, no new dependencies)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The feature is nominal and documentary, so it renames in place and adds only one contract suite; creating a module, dependency or data structure would violate the spec constraints and Principles I and II."}, {"id": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_plan_filerenamecontracttest_phase_aware_refactor", "label": "FileRenameContractTest Phase-Aware Refactor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The suite already encodes history for feature 009 (regras-* -> como-*) and 04 (template-*), so it is refactored into p1LegacyOld/p1Current/p1New instead of being rewritten, preserving historical coverage while adding the new layer."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_plan_implementation_plan", "target": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_plan_three_phase_fasing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/plan.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_plan_implementation_plan", "target": "specs_011_rename_contract_rule_files_plan_constitution_check", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "specs/011-rename-contract-rule-files/plan.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_011_rename_contrac